  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 189, 'Ask a peer to swap feedback on a small piece of work, each offering one thing that works and one thing to try.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 190, 'When a stranger criticizes you online, remind yourself that they are responding to a sliver of who you are.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 191, 'Tell a coworker what kind of feedback helps you most, such as direct, written or in person.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 192, 'Rest your eyes for one minute after a critical comment, then open them and decide your next step.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 193, 'Write one sentence that describes what you want people to feel when they give you feedback.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 194, 'Look for the question behind a complaint, like "Can I count on you?" and answer that question directly.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 195, 'Ask your partner to tell you gently when you seem defensive, and agree on a word they can use.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 196, 'Let one small criticism go unanswered today, trusting that your actions will speak over time.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 197, 'Before bed, list any comment still on your mind and write one kind response to your own replay of it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 198, 'Ask a helpful question in response to criticism, such as "What would you suggest?", rather than defending your choice.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 199, 'Picture your younger self receiving a comment you got today, and notice how gently you would want them treated.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 200, 'Notice any criticism you have been avoiding hearing, and make a plan to invite it on your own terms.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 201, 'When a coach, trainer or teammate corrects your form, try the suggestion right away before deciding if it helps.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 202, 'Admit one mistake at work plainly today, without softening it with extra explanation.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 203, 'Walk around the block during lunch after receiving feedback, and on the way back choose one thing to do with it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 204, 'Ask a longtime friend, "Is there anything I could do better as a friend?" and receive the answer with thanks.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 205, 'Hear a piece of criticism fully, then ask yourself, "Would I still care about this in a year?"'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 206, 'Notice how the people you admire take feedback, and borrow one of their habits today.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 207, 'Write down one piece of feedback you disagree with and one reasonable person who might agree with it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 208, 'Wait until a heated moment passes before responding to a relative''s criticism, even if that means saying nothing now.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 209, 'Ask for feedback at the start of a project by sharing a rough outline instead of waiting until it is finished.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 210, 'When a comment comes with a sharp edge, respond to the point and let the edge go unmentioned.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 211, 'Make a small change in response to feedback from someone at home, and let them notice it without announcing it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 212, 'Remind yourself that people who give feedback often feel nervous too, and thank them for taking that risk.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 213, 'Notice any tightness in your throat during a critical talk and swallow slowly to release it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 214, 'Choose a critical comment about your appearance and decide deliberately whether it deserves any space in your mind.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 215, 'Ask a group you belong to, like a club or class, what one thing would make your contribution more helpful.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 216, 'When you feel judged by a glance or silence, check whether any criticism was actually said out loud.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 217, 'Give a friend feedback they asked for, being specific and kind, and notice how careful you want to be.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 218, 'Say "Can you say more about that?" the next time a comment surprises you.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 219, 'At the end of a long week, write a short list of the feedback worth keeping and let the rest go with the weekend.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 220, 'Start your morning by deciding that today you will treat every piece of feedback as a possible gift worth opening.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 221, 'Ask a coworker what they found confusing about your last presentation, and write down the answer without comment.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 222, 'When a family member offers unwanted advice, say "I appreciate you caring," and let that be enough.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 223, 'Take a slow breath in for four counts and out for six the moment you notice defensiveness rising.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 224, 'Pick a spot in your home, like the front door, where you mentally leave behind criticism from the outside world.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 225, 'Ask a partner what they meant by a sigh or look, instead of assuming it was criticism.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 226, 'Try to find the one word in a piece of feedback that matters most, and focus your response on it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 227, 'Notice when you want to point out that the critic makes mistakes too, and set that thought aside for now.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 228, 'Accept one suggestion today on the spot, without asking why or explaining your original choice.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 229, 'Imagine the feedback you received is written on a leaf floating down a stream, and watch it drift away for a minute.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 230, 'Ask a coworker or friend for one tip on something you are learning, and use it right away.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 231, 'Look over a set of online comments on something you shared and count how many are neutral or kind.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 232, 'When criticism comes in a loud voice, keep your own voice at its usual volume.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 233, 'Write out what happened in a critical exchange as a neutral news reporter would describe it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 234, 'Notice whether you invite feedback from people who agree with you, and ask someone with a different view this time.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 235, 'On a warm day, eat lunch outside and let the change of scene loosen the grip of a morning comment.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 236, 'Make a list of the kinds of feedback you find hardest to hear, and choose one to practice with gently.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 237, 'Answer a critical email with a brief summary of the request and a date you will follow up.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 238, 'Ask your child, niece or nephew what you could do better at a game you play together, and laugh along with the answer.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 239, 'When you get conflicting feedback from two people, write down what each one values before choosing a path.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 240, 'Treat the next critique as a puzzle: what is the problem they see, and is there a fix you can try?'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 241, 'Think about the last time you criticized someone, and notice how much you hoped they would listen.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 242, 'Say out loud "I''m not going to argue about this," and mean it, when a remark is not worth debating.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 243, 'Carry a small object in your pocket today, like a smooth stone, and touch it when a comment stings.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 244, 'Ask someone who reviewed your work which change they think would make the biggest difference.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 245, 'Notice any feedback you have been storing up as proof against yourself, and choose to look at it fresh.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 246, 'Spend a quiet five minutes after dinner writing down one useful point you heard today.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 247, 'Ask for a specific example when someone calls you "always late" or "never listening," so you can see the real pattern.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 248, 'When criticized in a store, restaurant or line, respond with one polite sentence and step away.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 249, 'Let a friend know that a comment they made hurt, calmly and without blame, so you are not left replaying it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 250, 'Tell the person who gave you feedback what you plan to do with it, even if the plan is small.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 251, 'Look at a piece of criticism from the other person''s side and write what pressures they might be under.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 252, 'Keep your response to criticism under three sentences today, and notice how that feels.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 253, 'Plan a short reward for yourself after a feedback conversation you have been dreading.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 254, 'Ask a peer who handles criticism well how they keep from taking it personally.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 255, 'Hear out an entire complaint from a family member without planning your answer, then ask what they need.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 256, 'Name one criticism that pushed you to do something better, and send a quick note of thanks to its source if you can.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 257, 'When feedback arrives while you are tired or hungry, eat or rest first before deciding what it means.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 258, 'Take a pause in conversation by saying, "Give me a second to take that in."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 259, 'Ask your manager or a senior coworker, "What would it look like if I did this at the next level?"'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 260, 'Sit quietly for three minutes after feedback, noticing sounds around you rather than the words you heard.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 261, 'Spot one comment you took as criticism today that may simply have been a preference, and file it that way.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 262, 'Practice saying no to a suggestion you have weighed and rejected, kindly and without a long reason.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 263, 'Write a letter you will not send to someone whose criticism hurt, then tear it up or delete it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 264, 'Ask a fellow volunteer or teammate how your part of a shared task could go more smoothly.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 265, 'Notice if a comment triggers an old memory, and remind yourself that the present moment is different.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 266, 'When a partner criticizes you during an argument, focus on one sentence you can agree with and say so.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 267, 'On a chilly morning, bundle up for a short outdoor stroll and use it to decide which recent feedback is worth keeping.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 268, 'Offer to hear feedback on how you handled a recent disagreement from the other person involved.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 269, 'Remember one piece of criticism that turned out to be completely wrong, and notice that you survived it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 270, 'When a critic has a point but a harsh delivery, say, "You''re right about that part."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 271, 'Spend a few minutes tidying your workspace after a tough review, giving your mind a small, calm win.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 272, 'Ask yourself whether a criticism is a request, an opinion or a fact, and respond to it in that spirit.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 273, 'Notice how often you say "I know" when given advice, and try "Thanks" instead today.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 274, 'Send a thank-you to a reviewer, editor or colleague who took time to comment on your work.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 275, 'When your mind replays a harsh comment at night, jot it on a bedside pad and tell yourself you can look again in the morning.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 276, 'Ask your closest friend, "What do you think I''m too hard on myself about when people give me feedback?"'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 277, 'Resist the urge to seek reassurance from others right after criticism, and sit with it on your own for ten minutes first.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 278, 'Look at your calendar and schedule a short check-in to ask for feedback on something you are working on.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 279, 'Say "That''s a good catch" when someone finds an error in your work.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 280, 'Choose one critic in your life whose opinion you no longer need to give much weight, and quietly lower the volume.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 281, 'Talk to yourself in the second person after a hard comment: "You''re doing fine, you can take what helps."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 282, 'Try a new approach someone suggested, just once, and see how it goes before judging it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 283, 'Notice whether the feedback you are replaying is actually about something that can still change.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 284, 'Ask a friend who has had a similar job or role how they would have handled the feedback you got.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 285, 'Before a holiday gathering, decide on one topic you will gently steer away from if it brings criticism.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 286, 'Give feedback to a service provider this week in a kind, specific way, and see how they receive it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 287, 'Put a hand on your belly and feel it rise and fall while someone tells you something hard to hear.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 288, 'Choose one sentence of critical feedback and look up any word in it you are unsure about, so you understand it exactly.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 289, 'Ask your partner to share one thing you did this month that they appreciated and one thing they would like more of.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 290, 'Reflect on whether the way you took feedback today matches the person you are trying to be.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 291, 'When you realize you were wrong after defending yourself, go back and say, "You were right, I''m sorry I pushed back."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 292, 'Share a recent mistake with a coworker and ask how they would approach it, inviting feedback on your fix.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 293, 'Wake up and name one conversation today where you might hear feedback, then picture yourself staying steady through it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 294, 'Ask a friend to watch a short video or listen to a voice note of you speaking and offer one tip.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 295, 'When a relative criticizes your parenting, cooking or career, answer with a question about their own experience.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 296, 'Notice when criticism makes you want to quit something, and wait a full day before deciding.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 297, 'Pull out one old comment you still carry and weigh it: is it useful, partly useful or not useful today?'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 298, 'Try the three-breath rule: three slow breaths between any critical sentence you hear and your first reply.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 299, 'Ask the person to repeat a comment if you only half heard it, instead of filling in the worst version.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 300, 'Mentally sort the feedback you got this week into piles for work, home and everything else.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 301, 'Notice which person''s criticism affects you most, and think about why their opinion carries so much weight.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 302, 'Choose a moment this afternoon to ask one coworker how your recent handoff or update could be clearer.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 303, 'When you cannot change the thing criticized, say so calmly: "I can''t change that, but I hear you."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 304, 'Lie down for a few minutes after an intense feedback meeting and let your muscles go heavy.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 305, 'Name out loud one thing you learned from the last person who disagreed with you.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 306, 'When a comment is only partly fair, thank the person for the fair part and quietly skip the rest.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 307, 'Invite one friend to tell you if something you post online comes across differently than you intend.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 308, 'Practice letting silence sit for a few seconds after a criticism instead of rushing to fill it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 309, 'Ask a customer or reader, "Is there anything that would have made this better for you?"'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 310, 'Notice how you react when someone criticizes a person you love, and use it to understand how critics feel protective too.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 311, 'Write a short list of feedback you have acted on over the years, and let it remind you that you can grow.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 312, 'When you feel misunderstood by a critic, restate what you meant once, calmly, and then let it rest.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 313, 'Choose a spring or summer evening to sit outside and reflect on a comment that has been following you around.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 314, 'Go through one feedback conversation in your head and pick the single best moment of how you handled it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 315, 'Ask your partner, "When I get defensive, what would help you feel heard?"'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 316, 'Stop yourself from scrolling back through a critical thread once you have read it fully.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 317, 'When feedback touches a sensitive topic, say, "This is a tender spot for me, so give me a moment."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 318, 'Get curious about someone who criticized you by asking what led them to see it that way.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 319, 'Give yourself one full minute of kind attention after receiving criticism, like you would for a friend who stubbed a toe.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 320, 'Ask for feedback on a new skill early and often, framing it as "I''m still learning, what should I try next?"'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 321, 'Pay attention to your hands during a critical conversation and rest them open on your lap or the table.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 322, 'Reread a message that upset you after a night''s sleep, and notice what has changed in how you read it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 323, 'Tell a coworker, "I''d rather hear it from you directly," to make honest feedback easier for them to give.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 324, 'Notice any criticism you give yourself that was first said by someone else, and decide whether you still agree.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 325, 'When feedback arrives at a busy time, jot "look at later" on it and give it proper attention once things calm down.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 326, 'Ask a friend who knows you well to name one thing you could let go of hearing as criticism.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 327, 'Try responding to a critical online review of your work with a short thank-you and one concrete fix.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 328, 'Observe a conversation where someone else receives criticism, and note what helps or hinders them.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 329, 'Soften your forehead and let your eyebrows relax while you listen to a comment you dislike.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 330, 'Ask a family member what small change they think would make home life feel easier, and try it this week.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 331, 'Explain to someone what you took from their feedback, so they know it landed.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 332, 'Choose one comment from today and decide in writing to keep it, adjust it or discard it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 333, 'Decide ahead of a performance review which two questions you will ask to get specific next steps.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 334, 'Resist forwarding a critical message to friends for sympathy right away, and read it alone once more first.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 335, 'Hum or breathe slowly through your nose for a minute when a comment leaves you rattled.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 336, 'Invite a coworker to name one habit of yours in meetings that could be distracting, and thank them warmly.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 337, 'When a stranger gives you unsolicited advice in public, smile, say "Thanks," and carry on with your day.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 338, 'List two things a recent critic got right about you and one thing they missed.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 339, 'Practice giving feedback to yourself in the same calm tone you would like to hear from others.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 340, 'Ask someone for feedback on your feedback: "Was that helpful, or did it come across too sharply?"'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 341, 'Picture the criticism you are replaying shrinking to the size of a postage stamp, and set it aside.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 342, 'When someone at home criticizes the way you load the dishwasher or fold towels, try their way once.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 343, 'Put a sticky note on your mirror that reads "Take what helps, leave the rest."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 344, 'Ask a client, customer or colleague to rate one small part of your service, and thank them for their time.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 345, 'Before replying to criticism, check whether you are responding to the words or to how tired you are.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 346, 'Take a short break to drink something warm and notice the taste, then return to the feedback with fresh eyes.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 347, 'Seek out one piece of feedback on something you are already good at, to keep growing where you feel confident.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 348, 'When you notice yourself taking a critic''s side against yourself, speak up for yourself kindly in your head.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 349, 'Ask someone you have given feedback to how it felt to receive it, and learn from what they say.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 350, 'Allow a comment to be true without making it big: "Yes, I missed that, and it is fixable."'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 351, 'At the end of the day, write the words "enough for today" and close any open feedback files or messages.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 352, 'Say "Good point" to someone who questions your plan, and then decide calmly whether to change it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 353, 'Notice any comments about you from people who do not know you well, and give them less room in your mind.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 354, 'Ask a teammate for a quick gut reaction to an idea before you polish it, so feedback comes cheaply.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 355, 'When your partner offers a critique, thank them for trusting you with it before you respond.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 356, 'Imagine explaining a recent critique to a curious child, using plain, simple words without blame.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 357, 'During the autumn season, rake leaves or sweep a path, letting each stroke clear away one old comment.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 358, 'Share with someone who once criticized you how their feedback changed what you do.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 359, 'Before a hard conversation, take a minute to picture yourself calm, listening and asking one good question.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 360, 'Notice the relief that comes when you stop defending a small point, and let yourself enjoy it.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 361, 'Write down the kindest possible reason someone might have given you the criticism you are thinking about.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 362, 'When faced with a personal attack rather than feedback, choose silence or a calm exit over a reply.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 363, 'Ask a mentor or trusted friend to tell you one blind spot they have noticed, then thank them sincerely.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 364, 'Look back over this challenge and write down three ways you now hear criticism differently.'),
  ('taking-criticism-in-stride', 365, 'Close today by naming one piece of feedback you are glad you heard, and one you are glad you let go.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 1, 'Write down three things that are yours alone, outside of caregiving, and put the list where you will see it tonight.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 2, 'Sit down for five minutes with a cup of something warm before the next task, and let the task wait.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 3, 'Drink a full glass of water before you pour one for the person you care for.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 4, 'Name one feeling you have about caregiving right now, out loud or on paper, without deciding whether it is fair.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 5, 'Text one friend a single line about your own day, not about the person you care for.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 6, 'Start a note on your phone called "What helps" and add one thing that made today a little easier.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 7, 'Ask one specific person to handle one specific errand this week, and give them the day and the details.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 8, 'Hold the hand of the person you care for for one minute, with no task attached.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 9, 'Look up the phone number for a caregiver support line in your area and save it in your contacts.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 10, 'Step outside your front door for three minutes of fresh air while the person you care for is settled.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 11, 'Choose one small request you can answer with "not today" and say it kindly.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 12, 'Eat something with protein at lunch, sitting down, even if it is only a handful of nuts and a piece of cheese.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 13, 'Spend ten minutes on a hobby you set aside, even if all you do is open the box it lives in.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 14, 'Send your siblings a short message listing the three tasks that take most of your week.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 15, 'Put a folder by the door for the next appointment and drop in the insurance card and medication list.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 16, 'Go to bed fifteen minutes earlier than usual tonight, and leave the dishes if you must.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 17, 'Stretch your arms over your head and roll your shoulders while the kettle boils.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 18, 'When someone says "let me know if you need anything," answer with one real thing they can do.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 19, 'Notice a moment of resentment today and tell yourself, "That makes sense," before moving on.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 20, 'Ask the person you care for about a favorite song from when they were young, and play it together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 21, 'Search online for respite care in your county and write down one option to call later.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 22, 'Call a friend while you fold laundry, and talk about something that has nothing to do with caregiving.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 23, 'Pick one household chore to lower the standard on this week, and let it be good enough.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 24, 'Write the date of your own last checkup on a sticky note, and if it has been over a year, call to book one.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 25, 'Take a slow walk around the block, even if it is only the length of one podcast segment.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 26, 'Tell one family member exactly what would help most this month, in one sentence.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 27, 'Keep a small snack and a water bottle in the bag you carry to appointments, just for you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 28, 'Read two pages of a book you chose for yourself before you fall asleep.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 29, 'Let yourself cry for a few minutes if it comes, then wash your face with cool water.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 30, 'Invite the person you care for to teach you something they know, like a recipe or a card game.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 31, 'Write a list of questions for the next appointment so you do not have to hold them in your head.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 32, 'Say no to one extra commitment outside the house this week that you do not have room for.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 33, 'Find one support group for caregivers near you, in person or online, and note when it meets.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 34, 'Open a window in the morning and take five slow breaths of outside air.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 35, 'Choose one evening this week to be off duty for one hour, and ask someone to cover it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 36, 'Put on music you love while you do a caregiving task, chosen for you, not for them.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 37, 'Notice where your body is tense right now, and let that spot soften for three breaths.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 38, 'Write one sentence about who you were before caregiving began, and one about who you still are.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 39, 'Share a cup of tea with the person you care for and talk about the weather, the birds or nothing at all.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 40, 'Set a timer for a ten minute rest after lunch and lie down, even if you do not sleep.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 41, 'Ask a neighbor if they would pick up one item for you the next time they go to the store.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 42, 'Write down the name of one grief you carry about how things have changed.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 43, 'Go through today''s mail in one sitting, sort it into three piles, and set the rest aside.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 44, 'Wear something today that you like, not just what is practical.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 45, 'Tell a sibling one thing you appreciate about their help, then name one more thing you need.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 46, 'Put your own prescriptions and vitamins in the same spot as theirs so you remember yours too.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 47, 'Keep a paper calendar on the fridge with appointments, so everyone in the house can see the plan.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 48, 'Ask yourself, "What do I need in the next hour?" and do one small piece of the answer.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 49, 'Plan one thing to look forward to this week, however small, and write it on the calendar.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 50, 'Eat breakfast before you help anyone else with theirs.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 51, 'Look at an old photo with the person you care for and ask them to tell you the story behind it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 52, 'Set your cell phone to silent for twenty minutes and rest your eyes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 53, 'Tell a trusted friend one honest thing about how caregiving is going, without tidying it up.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 54, 'Make a list of the people who have offered help in the past year, even vaguely.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 55, 'Take the long way to the pharmacy if it passes somewhere pretty, and notice one thing you like.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 56, 'Find out if your workplace offers any family leave or flexible hours, and write down who to ask.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 57, 'Replace "I should" with "I could" in one thought about caregiving today.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 58, 'Give your own hands some lotion after the day''s washing and cleaning.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 59, 'Choose one meal this week to make simple, like soup and bread, and call it a win.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 60, 'Find out what the person you care for would like to do for fun this week, and do one piece of it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 61, 'Spend five minutes in the sun, on a porch, a step or by a bright window.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 62, 'Notice one thing you did well as a caregiver today, and say it to yourself plainly.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 63, 'Write down the password and account details for one bill you manage, in a safe place.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 64, 'Let one phone call go to voicemail today, and return it when you have the energy.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 65, 'Write a short note to yourself for the hard evenings: "You are doing a lot, and it is okay to rest."'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 66, 'Stand at the sink and do ten slow heel raises while the water runs.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 67, 'Call a sibling and suggest one regular task they could take over for good, like a weekly call or a bill.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 68, 'Put fresh flowers, a leaf or a pinecone where the person you care for can see it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 69, 'Look up whether your area has adult day programs, and jot down one name.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 70, 'Plan a phone date with an old friend for a time you know is usually quiet.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 71, 'Take a shower that lasts a little longer than it needs to, and let it be rest.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 72, 'Say, "I can do that on Thursday, not today," to one request that can wait.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 73, 'Write down one thing you miss about your life before caregiving, and one small way to touch it this month.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 74, 'Offer the person you care for one small choice today, like a shirt or a snack, and let it be theirs.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 75, 'Keep a glass of water by the chair where you sit most, and finish it before dinner.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 76, 'Write down the one caregiving task that drains you most, and brainstorm one way to share it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 77, 'Spend fifteen minutes on your own interest after the evening routine, before you reach for chores.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 78, 'Tell yourself, "I am allowed to feel tired of this and still love them."'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 79, 'Ask a friend to sit with the person you care for for an hour so you can go somewhere alone.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 80, 'Make a simple chart of weekly medications so anyone who helps can follow it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 81, 'Walk to the mailbox slowly and look up at the sky on the way.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 82, 'Cancel or postpone one thing on your own calendar that is more duty than joy.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 83, 'Read the person you care for a short poem, article or letter, and just enjoy the sound of it together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 84, 'Call the office that handles one bill or benefit, and ask them to explain one thing you do not understand.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 85, 'Write down your own sleep time tonight and wake time tomorrow, just to see what you are getting.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 86, 'Put one reminder in your phone for a friend''s birthday, and plan a short message for it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 87, 'Notice guilt when you rest, name it, and rest anyway for five more minutes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 88, 'Ask the pharmacy whether they can sync refill dates so pickups happen once a month.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 89, 'Choose a comfortable pair of shoes for the busiest day of your week.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 90, 'Sit in your car for three quiet minutes before you walk into the next appointment.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 91, 'Ask a family member to be the point person for one type of call, like insurance or the pharmacy.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 92, 'Share a funny memory with the person you care for, and laugh about it together if you can.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 93, 'Write down three signs that tell you your own tank is getting low.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 94, 'Eat one piece of fruit today that you actually enjoy, slowly.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 95, 'Look up whether your local library or community center has a caregiver program or resource list.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 96, 'Write back to one friend you have been meaning to answer, even with a short reply.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 97, 'Find a five minute stretch routine you can do on the floor beside the bed, and try it once.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 98, 'Say "Thank you, yes," the next time someone offers help, instead of "I''m fine."'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 99, 'Keep one drawer or shelf in the house that belongs only to your things.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 100, 'Draw, doodle or color for five minutes while the person you care for rests.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 101, 'Ask the doctor''s office if a nurse line is available for questions between visits, and save the number.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 102, 'Take one hour this week where you leave your phone on and still do something just for you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 103, 'Write a text to a sibling that begins, "Here is what I need from you this month."'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 104, 'Let yourself be sad about one thing that is lost, without trying to fix it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 105, 'Rub lotion into the hands of the person you care for, slowly, as a moment of closeness.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 106, 'Book one appointment for your own teeth, eyes or ears that you have put off.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 107, 'Put a timer on your phone for a mid-afternoon glass of water and a stretch.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 108, 'Tell one person at work or church that you are caregiving, so they understand your limits.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 109, 'Listen to one song all the way through with your eyes closed.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 110, 'Write the name and number of every doctor the person you care for sees on one page.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 111, 'Ask yourself what you would tell a friend in your shoes, and say one of those things to yourself.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 112, 'Take a nap on the weekend if a window opens, and do not make it up afterward.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 113, 'Ask a grown child, niece or nephew to visit for an afternoon and spell out what would help.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 114, 'Answer one request with, "Let me check my week and get back to you."'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 115, 'Water a plant, feed the birds or tend something small that is yours.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 116, 'Say out loud one thing you are angry about, alone in the car or the shower, and let it pass.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 117, 'Put together a small bag for your own waiting room time: a book, a snack, earbuds.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 118, 'Watch the sunset or the sunrise from wherever you are, for as long as it takes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 119, 'Trade one thing you are each grateful for today with the person you care for.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 120, 'Write down one hope you have for yourself in the next year, separate from caregiving.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 121, 'Invite a friend to walk with you while you run an errand together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 122, 'Pack your lunch the night before a long appointment day.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 123, 'Look into whether a volunteer driver program serves your area for rides to appointments.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 124, 'Tell a friend you would love a short visit, and suggest a time that works.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 125, 'Brush your hair, wash your face and put on something fresh before the afternoon starts.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 126, 'Give yourself permission to skip one optional task today, and write "skipped on purpose" beside it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 127, 'Sit on the edge of the bed with the person you care for and look out the window together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 128, 'Divide one shared chore between you and a sibling with clear dates, and put it in writing.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 129, 'Take five slow breaths before you answer the phone when a family member calls.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 130, 'Keep one evening snack in the house that is just for you, and enjoy it without sharing.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 131, 'Make a list of small jobs that visitors could do in ten minutes, and keep it by the door.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 132, 'Ask a caregiver you know how they manage one hard part of the week.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 133, 'Write for five minutes about what today felt like, then close the notebook.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 134, 'Try one gentle exercise video for ten minutes in the living room.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 135, 'Ask the doctor to write down the plan in plain words before you leave the next visit.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 136, 'Look for a quiet corner in the house that can be your rest spot, and put a pillow there.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 137, 'Call your own doctor''s office and ask whether any screenings are due for you this year.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 138, 'Read the paper, a magazine or a favorite blog for ten minutes over coffee, just for you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 139, 'Plan an easy supper for tomorrow tonight, so tomorrow asks less of you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 140, 'Tell someone who helped you this week exactly how their help made a difference.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 141, 'Hand the choice of tonight''s show or music to the person you care for, and enjoy it beside them.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 142, 'Notice a moment when you feel impatient, pause, and take one long breath before speaking.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 143, 'Find a nearby park bench and sit on it for ten minutes this week.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 144, 'Ask a friend to check in on you by text once a week, on a set day.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 145, 'Write down which part of the day is hardest, and think of one small change that might ease it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 146, 'Say no to hosting one gathering this season, and suggest someone else take a turn.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 147, 'Before a holiday, decide on one tradition to keep and one to let go of this year.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 148, 'Ask a relative to host the next family holiday meal, and offer to bring one dish instead.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 149, 'On a warm afternoon, take the person you care for outside for a few minutes of sun together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 150, 'On a cold morning, warm your own hands on a mug and let yourself sit before the day begins.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 151, 'In spring, plant one seed or small plant in a pot, and let caring for it be a quiet pleasure.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 152, 'Choose one holiday card to send to an old friend, and write a real sentence in it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 153, 'Tell family ahead of a holiday what you can and cannot manage this year.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 154, 'Serve a seasonal food the person you care for loves this week, and share it slowly together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 155, 'Plan a short break for yourself in the days after a busy holiday, before you need it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 156, 'Watch the first snow, rain or falling leaves out the window for a few minutes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 157, 'Buy yourself one small thing for a holiday, and wrap it if you like.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 158, 'On a long summer evening, sit outside alone for ten minutes after the person you care for is in bed.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 159, 'Ask a sibling to take the lead on birthday plans for your parent this year.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 160, 'Hang one seasonal decoration that makes you happy, and skip the rest if you are tired.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 161, 'Make a short list of what made last year''s holidays hard, and change one thing on it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 162, 'On a rainy day, light a candle or turn on a lamp and let the room feel cozy for you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 163, 'Invite a friend for a slice of pie or a cup of cocoa during the holiday season, even for half an hour.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 164, 'Invite a story about what a holiday meant to the person you care for as a child, and listen.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 165, 'Set a spending limit for holiday gifts that protects your own energy and budget.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 166, 'On the first mild day of spring, open the windows and let fresh air through the house.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 167, 'Choose one fall walk to take by yourself, and notice the colors of the leaves.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 168, 'Keep one holiday evening free of caregiving tasks by asking another family member to cover.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 169, 'Look at the calendar for the coming season and mark your own rest days first.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 170, 'Take a picture of something beautiful this season that has nothing to do with caregiving.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 171, 'Include the person you care for in a small seasonal task, like stirring batter or sorting cards.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 172, 'Order one holiday gift online instead of going to a crowded store.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 173, 'Before summer heat arrives, put a cold drink in the fridge just for you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 174, 'Let a holiday be quieter than it used to be, and say so plainly to anyone who asks.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 175, 'Mark your own birthday on the calendar and plan one thing you will do for yourself.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 176, 'Sing along to one seasonal song with the person you care for, even off-key.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 177, 'Leave the phone inside and step onto the porch to feel the evening temperature.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 178, 'Send a group text to your siblings before a holiday with a clear sign-up list of tasks.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 179, 'When the clocks change, go to bed at your new time and give your body a few days to adjust.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 180, 'Notice if the holidays bring up grief, and set aside a few minutes to let it be there.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 181, 'Pack a picnic lunch on a nice day and eat it outside with the person you care for.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 182, 'Ask a neighbor to shovel, rake or mow once this season, and offer to return the favor later.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 183, 'Plan one easy meal for a holiday weekend so you are not cooking all day.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 184, 'Wear something warm and soft on a chilly evening and let it feel like care for you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 185, 'Write down one memory from a past holiday with the person you care for that you want to keep.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 186, 'Plan a short outing in a season you love, even just a drive to see the trees or lights.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 187, 'Give the person you care for a small seasonal treat, like a fresh peach or a mug of cider, and enjoy it with them.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 188, 'Say yes to one holiday invitation for yourself, and arrange cover so you can go.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 189, 'Ask the doctor''s office for flu shot times for both of you, and book yours too.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 190, 'Check that your own winter boots, coat and gloves are ready before the cold arrives.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 191, 'Let one holiday tradition shrink to its simplest version, like one batch of cookies instead of five.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 192, 'On a summer morning, take your coffee outside before anyone else is awake.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 193, 'Call a friend on a holiday you usually spend busy, and wish them well for two minutes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 194, 'When the new year comes, write one wish for yourself on a slip of paper and keep it in your wallet.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 195, 'Tell a sibling which holiday you need them to cover this year, by name and date.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 196, 'On a gray afternoon, open the curtains wide and let in as much daylight as you can.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 197, 'Spend a few minutes looking through seed catalogs, travel photos or recipes for next season.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 198, 'Make a quiet plan for a hard anniversary, like calling a friend or taking a walk.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 199, 'Put on sunscreen and a hat for yourself before an outdoor errand, not just for them.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 200, 'Offer to take a family photo at a holiday gathering, and step into one yourself.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 201, 'Rest for twenty minutes after a holiday visit, before you start cleaning up.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 202, 'Look up whether any local groups hold caregiver events or respite days around the holidays.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 203, 'Share one seasonal smell with the person you care for, like pine, cinnamon or cut grass.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 204, 'Set out a bowl of fruit in the season''s colors and help yourself first.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 205, 'Ask a friend to go to one seasonal event with you, like a market or a concert in the park.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 206, 'Keep a warm blanket by your own chair for evenings, not only by theirs.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 207, 'On a hot day, stay inside for the midday hours and let the errands wait until evening.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 208, 'Write a short thank you to someone who helped over a busy season.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 209, 'Let yourself say, "This holiday is hard for me," to one person who can hear it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 210, 'Take a few minutes in late summer to plan your own fall checkups before the season fills.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 211, 'Gather a few autumn leaves or spring blossoms and set them where the person you care for can see them.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 212, 'Make a pot of soup on a cold day and freeze a few portions for tired evenings.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 213, 'Ask yourself which season has always given you energy, and plan one small thing in it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 214, 'On a clear night, step outside to look at the moon or the stars for a minute.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 215, 'Tell your family, before the holiday, one thing you would like to receive: time off, a meal or a visit.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 216, 'Take down one holiday decoration at a time instead of all in one tiring afternoon.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 217, 'When a new season starts, swap one piece of your routine for something fresh.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 218, 'Sit with the person you care for and watch a holiday parade, a game or a special on TV together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 219, 'Read one seasonal poem or passage to yourself on a quiet morning.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 220, 'Scan one important document, like an insurance card or ID, into your phone so it is always with you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 221, 'Ask the pharmacist to explain one medication, so you feel less alone with the details.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 222, 'Make a one page summary of the health history of the person you care for, to hand to new doctors.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 223, 'Write down every appointment for the next two weeks in one place, and circle the busiest day.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 224, 'Ask whether the next appointment can be a phone or video visit, to save a trip.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 225, 'Keep a pen and notepad in the car for notes at appointments.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 226, 'Set a reminder a week before each bill is due, and let the phone remember for you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 227, 'Ask a sibling to go through one stack of paperwork with you on a video call.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 228, 'Bring someone with you to one important appointment, so you have a second pair of ears.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 229, 'Label one folder for each area, like medical, money and home, and file one paper in each.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 230, 'Ask the front desk for the name of one person you can call with scheduling questions.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 231, 'Write down the three questions you most want answered before the next visit, in order.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 232, 'Find out who to call if the regular doctor is closed, and put that number on the fridge.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 233, 'Take a photo of the appointment card before you leave the office.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 234, 'Ask the social worker or care coordinator at a clinic or hospital what help is available for families.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 235, 'Put a small notebook in the bag you take to appointments, just for your own thoughts in the waiting room.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 236, 'Book two appointments on the same day in the same building if you can, to save a trip.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 237, 'Ask whether any forms can be filled out online ahead of the visit.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 238, 'Ask a friend who is good with paperwork to look over one form with you.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 239, 'Clear one corner of the table for paperwork, so the rest of the house can stay calm.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 240, 'Schedule your own annual physical, and put it on the calendar in the same color as theirs.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 241, 'Ask your own doctor how caregiving might be affecting your sleep and energy.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 242, 'Get your own blood pressure checked at a pharmacy or clinic this month.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 243, 'Refill your own prescriptions before they run out, and set a reminder for next time.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 244, 'Tell your own doctor you are a caregiver, so they can ask about your stress and rest.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 245, 'Make a dentist appointment for yourself, and ask a family member to cover that hour.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 246, 'Notice one ache or pain you have been ignoring, and write it down for your next checkup.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 247, 'Book an eye exam if reading or driving has felt harder lately.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 248, 'Check that your own vaccines are up to date, and ask where to get any you need.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 249, 'Keep a short list of your own questions for your doctor in the same folder as theirs.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 250, 'Tell someone about one worry you have for your own health, instead of carrying it alone.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 251, 'Lie on the floor with your legs up on a chair for five minutes after a long stretch of standing.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 252, 'Take a warm bath or foot soak after a heavy day, and let the water do some of the work.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 253, 'Put your feet up while you eat lunch.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 254, 'Close your eyes for two minutes after hanging up a hard phone call.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 255, 'Go outside at dusk and listen to the sounds of the evening for five minutes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 256, 'Take a slow bite of something sweet and let it be a small pleasure.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 257, 'Find a quiet chair, sit, and do nothing at all for three minutes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 258, 'Take three deep breaths at every red light on the way to an appointment.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 259, 'Rest your head on a pillow for five minutes midafternoon, even if you do not lie down fully.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 260, 'Make a cup of tea and drink it while it is still hot, before you do anything else.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 261, 'Let the person you care for doze while you read beside them, and count it as rest for you too.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 262, 'Set up one small comfort in your car, like a soft scarf or a favorite playlist, for waiting times.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 263, 'Take a five minute pause after each meal you serve, before you clear the table.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 264, 'Turn off the news for a day and let your mind rest from it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 265, 'Go to bed with no screens for the last twenty minutes of the night.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 266, 'Take a quiet moment at the kitchen table before the house wakes up.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 267, 'Lean against a wall and let your shoulders drop, then take five long breaths.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 268, 'Look out a window at trees or sky for two minutes between tasks.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 269, 'Keep a soft pair of socks by the bed to put on the moment you lie down.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 270, 'Eat a real dinner at the table tonight, even if it is simple and you are alone.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 271, 'Keep a bowl of easy snacks like nuts, fruit or crackers where you can reach it between tasks.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 272, 'Refill your water bottle each time you refill theirs.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 273, 'Take a short walk after dinner, even five minutes to the corner and back.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 274, 'Do ten gentle squats, holding the kitchen counter, while waiting for the microwave.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 275, 'Make a big batch of one meal on a calmer day and freeze half for a harder one.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 276, 'Keep a protein bar and a bottle of water in the car for long days out.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 277, 'Notice when you last ate, and if it was more than four hours ago, eat something now.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 278, 'Stretch your neck gently side to side before you lift or help someone move.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 279, 'Ask a helper to show you a safer way to lift or move the person you care for, to protect your back.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 280, 'Put on your walking shoes and walk to the end of the street and back while someone else is home.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 281, 'Go to bed at the same time three nights in a row this week.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 282, 'Swap one sugary drink today for water with a slice of lemon or cucumber.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 283, 'Dance to one song in the kitchen, alone or with the person you care for.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 284, 'Write down how many hours of sleep you get this week, without judging the number.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 285, 'Ask whether an overnight helper or a family member could take one night so you can sleep through.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 286, 'Keep earplugs or an eye mask by your bed for nights when you are not on call.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 287, 'Take the stairs slowly and deliberately today, and feel your legs working.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 288, 'Cook one meal for yourself that you love, even if the person you care for eats something different.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 289, 'Eat a vegetable at every meal today, in whatever easy form you have.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 290, 'Spend five minutes stretching on the floor before bed.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 291, 'Go for a swim, bike ride or longer walk this week while someone else is on duty.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 292, 'Let yourself sleep in once this week if someone else can cover the morning.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 293, 'Look back over this challenge so far and circle the to-do that helped you most, then do it again.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 294, 'Pick up the knitting, sketchbook, guitar or puzzle you used to love, and give it ten minutes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 295, 'Sign up for one short class or online session in something you enjoy, even if it is months away.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 296, 'Listen to an episode of a podcast on a subject you love while you do the dishes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 297, 'Keep a small project, like a crossword or a craft, in the bag you take to appointments.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 298, 'Reread a few pages of a favorite old book from before caregiving began.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 299, 'Write a few lines of a poem, a story or a letter, just for the pleasure of it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 300, 'Bake something you enjoy baking, and keep one piece for yourself before sharing.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 301, 'Spend a few minutes learning one word in a language you always meant to study.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 302, 'Set up a weekly call with a friend who shares one of your interests, even for fifteen minutes.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 303, 'Share one thing you made or learned this week with someone who will be glad to hear it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 304, 'Plan one hobby hour in the next two weeks and ask someone to cover caregiving during it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 305, 'Send a voice message to a friend telling them one thing you miss about spending time together.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 306, 'Ask a friend to meet you for coffee near an appointment, while you wait.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 307, 'Reply to a group chat with something about your own life, not just caregiving news.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 308, 'Invite a friend over for a short visit and ask them to tell you about their life.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 309, 'Write a postcard to a friend who lives far away, and mail it today.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 310, 'Ask a friend what they are looking forward to this month, and really listen.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 311, 'Tell a friend, "I miss you, and I am still here," even if you cannot see them often.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 312, 'Accept one invitation this month, even if you can only stay for an hour.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 313, 'Put one friend''s name on the calendar for a call each month, and keep the date.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 314, 'Call a friend just to laugh about something, with no update required.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 315, 'Write down one feeling each evening this week, one word is enough.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 316, 'When you feel a flash of anger, name it quietly to yourself: "This is anger, and it will pass."'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 317, 'Notice a moment of loneliness today and reach out to one person because of it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 318, 'Allow yourself to feel relief when the person you care for is settled, without guilt.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 319, 'Write a letter to yourself about what you have given up, and do not send it to anyone.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 320, 'Say to yourself, "Both things are true: I love them, and this is hard."'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 321, 'Talk with a counselor, faith leader or trusted friend about the grief of watching someone change.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 322, 'Notice fear about the future, write it down, and put the paper away for the rest of the day.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 323, 'Let yourself feel proud of one hard thing you handled this week.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 324, 'Name one mixed feeling you have toward the person you care for, and let it be mixed.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 325, 'Reach for the hand of the person you care for and hold it for a moment, just because.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 326, 'Watch an old favorite movie together and let the story carry you both for a while.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 327, 'Brush the hair of the person you care for slowly, or let them brush yours, just for the closeness.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 328, 'Tell the person you care for one thing you love about them, in plain words.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 329, 'Sit together in silence for five minutes without trying to fill it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 330, 'Play a simple card game or board game with the person you care for, just for fun.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 331, 'Look through a photo album together and let them choose which pages to linger on.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 332, 'Seek the advice of the person you care for on something in your own life.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 333, 'Share a snack on the porch with the person you care for, with no schedule for it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 334, 'Laugh with the person you care for at something silly on TV or in the paper.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 335, 'Ask one friend or neighbor to bring a meal on a specific night this week.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 336, 'Ask a teenager in the family to spend an hour with the person you care for after school.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 337, 'Ask a church, club or community group member if they could visit once a month.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 338, 'Let a helper do a task their own way, as long as it is safe, and do not redo it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 339, 'Ask someone to drive one appointment this month, and use that time for yourself.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 340, 'Tell a visitor exactly how long you would like them to stay, so the visit fits your day.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 341, 'Turn down one request from a relative who does not help, politely and without a long explanation.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 342, 'Say "not right now" to a phone call that can wait, and call back when you have rested.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 343, 'Let one relative''s criticism pass without defending yourself, and change the subject.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 344, 'Kindly say to the person you care for that you need ten minutes to yourself, and take them.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 345, 'Set one hour each evening after which you do not answer non-urgent calls.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 346, 'Hold a short family call to talk about the months ahead, with a list of topics.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 347, 'Ask a sibling who lives far away to handle tasks that can be done by phone or online.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 348, 'Share your "What helps" list with a family member so they can step in more easily.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 349, 'Ask each family member to name one thing they can do regularly, and write their answers down.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 350, 'Suggest a rotation for weekend visits so one person is not always on call.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 351, 'Tell a sibling one way you would like to be thanked or supported, since they may not know.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 352, 'Add one new line to your list of what helps, whether it is a person, a place or a small routine.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 353, 'Read over your list of what helps on a hard day, and pick one thing from it.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 354, 'Write down one thing that did not help this week, so you can skip it next time.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 355, 'Visit one support group meeting, in person or online, and listen without needing to share.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 356, 'Call a caregiver line and ask what kinds of support are available where you live.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 357, 'Ask a local senior center or community center what respite options they know about.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 358, 'Find out whether short-term respite stays are available nearby, and what they involve.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 359, 'Ask another caregiver in a support group or online forum for one tip that worked for them.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 360, 'Look up whether your county has a family caregiver program, and write down its phone number.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 361, 'Glance back over this challenge so far, and write down the one habit you most want to keep.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 362, 'Plan your next free hour now, and decide what you will do with it for yourself.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 363, 'Write down one thing you have learned about yourself while caring for someone else.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 364, 'Tell someone you trust how you are really doing, and let them respond.'),
  ('caring-for-someone-without-losing-yourself', 365, 'Thank yourself tonight for the care you gave, and for the care you gave yourself.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
